I posted one comment, on #1002, and closed nothing. That issue stays open.

#1002 (prompt loaders getting around `--deny-dir`/`--allow-dir` through symlinks): this session's Task 1 (9348ada5, 36ae0cb8) fenced the channel where you name files in your own prompt.
• **What leaked:** I reproduced it first. With `--deny-dir` on the secret directory, both `@path` and `/add` still sent the target of a symlink in the denied directory to the model.
• **The fix:** the check now happens inside the two shared read functions, so every caller has to go through it. That also caught two places I hadn't listed: /explain and --image.
• **Tests:** they pass. When I deliberately disabled the check, exactly the 8 refusal tests failed and the 4 tests for normal, allowed reads still passed.
• **Still open:** the skills directories haven't been tested yet, and there's an undecided question about whether --safe-mode should skip the goal file.

